WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.158
Must things become unbearable before seeking help?

00:00:03.158 --> 00:00:06.316
A difficulty can be heard from the first sentence.

00:00:06.316 --> 00:00:09.474
Authoritative guidance describes routes to support.

00:00:09.474 --> 00:00:12.632
Trusted adults and professional services have different roles.

00:00:12.632 --> 00:00:15.789
You can ask about the process and share concerns.

00:00:15.789 --> 00:00:22.105
Describe what happened and for how long.

00:00:22.105 --> 00:00:28.421
Explain which parts of life are affected.

00:00:28.421 --> 00:00:34.737
Name one step where help is needed.

00:00:34.737 --> 00:00:41.053
This route map is educational, not triage.

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.211
No fixed waiting period is needed to voice concern.

00:00:44.211 --> 00:00:47.368
If one person misses it, seek another appropriate listener.

00:00:47.368 --> 00:00:50.526
For immediate danger, seek people who can ensure safety.

00:00:50.526 --> 00:00:56.842
You can describe sleep and activity changes.

00:00:56.842 --> 00:01:03.158
Ask to explore what support is available.

00:01:03.158 --> 00:01:06.316
Appropriate professionals assess health concerns.

00:01:06.316 --> 00:01:09.474
Seeking help need not reduce you to a label.

00:01:09.474 --> 00:01:12.632
Bring your questions into the process.

00:01:12.632 --> 00:01:15.789
The first sentence need not be perfect.
